# Embedded Python (AIBOM)

The CLI is primarily Go but **embeds a relocatable CPython runtime** and packaged
`cisco-aibom` for local `ai-bom analyze` — not a system Python dependency.

## Layout (post-migration)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `internal/embedded/python/` | `embed.go`, build tags, Go↔Python bridge |
| `internal/embedded/python/stub.go` | Stub build when embed disabled (CI/dev without bundle) |
| `scripts/` | Bundle scripts, `requirements-bundle.txt` |
| `Dockerfile` | Multi-stage: build CPython bundle + Go binary |

## Build tags

- **Full embed** — production/release binary with bundled interpreter + aibom
- **Stub** — `go test` / dev without downloading full CPython payload; tests must cover stub path

Do not break `go test ./...` on machines without the full Python bundle unless stub tag is default for tests.

## Python hygiene

- Pin versions in `requirements-bundle.txt` (or equivalent); no unpinned installs in release path
- `__pycache__/`, `.venv/`, and `internal/embedded/python/bundle/` are gitignored — never commit bundles
- Avoid `pickle` / unsafe deserialization; JSON and vetted aibom APIs only
- Do not shell out to arbitrary user Python; use only the embedded relocatable runtime

## Release impact

- Release artifacts must include the embedded runtime (single binary or documented layout)
- CI must build **both** stub (fast tests) and full embed (release smoke) where applicable
- Document platform support for embedded CPython (linux-amd64, darwin amd64/arm64)

